E["item:head-of-arugal"] = {t="item",n="Head of Arugal",z="shadowfang",s="At Shadowfang Keep, Head of Arugal is taken from the mad archmage who commands the worgen. The Forsaken at the Sepulcher seek it as proof that he has fallen.",h="At Shadowfang Keep, Head of Arugal is taken from the mad archmage who commands the worgen.",sec={{t="Trophy of the Mad Archmage",b="Archmage Arugal commands the worgen from Shadowfang Keep in Silverpine Forest. Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher gives the order to claim his severed head. The Forsaken see Arugal's fall as a blow against the beasts that hinder Lady Sylvanas's hold over Silverpine. Bringing the head to Dawnweaver proves the archmage's sorcery has been cut from the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants the Head of Arugal?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver, an emissary at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, wants the head as part of the order called Arugal Must Die.",al={"who needs arugals head","arugal head turn in","who takes head of arugal"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do you obtain the Head of Arugal?",a="The Head of Arugal comes from Archmage Arugal, who dwells at Shadowfang Keep's highest pinnacle, above Pyrewood Village and the Silverpine woods.",al={"how to get arugals head","arugal head drop","where is arugal's head"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken want Arugal dead?",a="The Forsaken want Arugal dead because he and his worgen pack keep them from securing Silverpine Forest as a safe stronghold for Lady Sylvanas and the Undercity.",al={"why kill arugal","forsaken arugal reason","why does dalar want arugal dead"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after the head is turned in?",a="After receiving the head, Dalar Dawnweaver vows to eradicate the remnants of Arugal's spells and declares Silverpine free of the mad wizard's grip.",al={"after arugal dies","result of arugal must die"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the Head of Arugal?",a="The Head of Arugal is the severed head of Archmage Arugal, the mad former wizard of Dalaran who unleashed the worgen upon Silverpine Forest. Taken from his fortress in Shadowfang Keep, it serves as undeniable physical proof that the crazed sorcerer has finally been slain and his dark magics broken.",al={"what is head of arugal","head of arugal item","arugal head"},it="identity",add="c9f64370"},{q="Where does the Head of Arugal come from?",a="The head is claimed directly from Archmage Arugal within the heights of Shadowfang Keep. After invading the cursed fortress and overcoming the mad archmage in battle, you strike him down and claim his head to confirm his demise.",al={"where do you get head of arugal","who drops head of arugal","arugals head origin"},it="origin",add="10305f38"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you help remove a dangerous sorcerer from the southern edge of Silverpine Forest and secure the land for the Dark Lady.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you see the severed head of a former Kirin Tor archmage as a warning of the madness and ruin that desperate summonings can bring, even to gifted practitioners."},kw={"arugal","arugal must die","dalar dawnweaver","head of arugal","sepulcher","shadowfang keep","silverpine"},rel={"npc:arugal","quest:1014","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","zone:shadowfang","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Head of Arugal","Arugal Must Die"}}
E["item:the-book-of-ur"] = {t="item",n="The Book of Ur",z="shadowfang",s="Ur's book now lies in Shadowfang Keep. Archmage Arugal took it after Ur died, and now Forsaken scholars in the Undercity take interest. The Dalaran mage wrote of strange beings from other planes.",h="Ur's book now lies in Shadowfang Keep.",sec={{t="The Mage of Dalaran",b="Ur was a Dalaran mage known for studying other planes and their creatures. Before the Scourge came, the Kirin Tor knew his work well. Ur was fascinated by magic beyond this world, yet he chose to write down his findings instead of breaking through the veil recklessly. Caution and restraint shaped his research. When the Scourge attacked Dalaran, neither his magic nor his care could save him.",sp=0},{t="Forsaken Ambition",b="After Ur's death, Archmage Arugal took his writings and used them to summon worgen into Silverpine Forest. The book now rests on a shelf in Shadowfang Keep. Keeper Bel'dugur of the Undercity's Apothecarium has heard of it and wants Ur's work. The Forsaken have none of Ur's restraint; they will use dangerous magic in their struggle to survive and conquer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Ur?",a="Ur was a human mage of Dalaran, known before the Third War for studying other dimensions and their creatures. He would not summon them, fearing the danger they posed.",al={"who wrote the book of ur","ur dalaran mage"},it="people"},{q="Where is the Book of Ur located?",a="The Book of Ur rests on a shelf in Shadowfang Keep, in Silverpine Forest, inside the chamber where the great beast Fenrus lives.",al={"book of ur location","where is book of ur"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Keeper Bel'dugur want the book?",a="Keeper Bel'dugur gathers Ur's writings for interested parties in the Undercity. The Forsaken believe Ur's conscience held back his power, and seek to use his research without ethical limits to strengthen themselves.",al={"keeper bel'dugur book of ur","why undercity wants the book"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How did the book end up in Shadowfang Keep?",a="After Ur died in Dalaran's fall, Archmage Arugal acquired his research. Seeking a way to defend against the Scourge, Arugal brought the notes to Silverpine Forest and used Ur's theories to summon worgen into Azeroth.",al={"arugal and book of ur","how did arugal get the book"},it="history"},{q="What is the Book of Ur?",a="The Book of Ur is a scholarly tome containing the esoteric research of Ur, an accomplished mage of Dalaran. It details his extensive studies into other worlds and dangerous arcane phenomena—knowledge that proved so potent that Archmage Arugal later used Ur's writings to summon the monstrous worgen into Silverpine Forest.",al={"what is book of ur","book of ur lore","what is the book of ur"},it="identity",add="62a01830"},{q="Where does the Book of Ur come from, and who made it?",a="The book was penned in the magical kingdom of Dalaran by the mage Ur prior to the Scourge's destruction of the city. Ur documented his arcane theories and explorations into other dimensions, though his work was abandoned following his demise during the fall of Dalaran.",al={"who wrote the book of ur","book of ur origin","where did the book of ur come from"},it="origin",add="905bb2c4"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, securing Ur's work aids the Dark Lady's scholars in the Apothecarium. A cautious human wizard's research may become practical power for the Forsaken.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, Ur's writings show how far Dalaran's scholars studied other realms, and the deadly cost when Arugal misused that forbidden knowledge."},kw={"apothecarium","arugal","book of ur","dalaran","keeper bel'dugur","shadowfang keep","silverpine","ur"},rel={"quest:1013","npc:arugal","npc:keeper-bel-dugur","zone:shadowfang","subzone:apothecarium","subzone:dalaran","topic:forsaken","zone:silverpine"},src={"The Book of Ur","The Book of Ur (quest)"}}
E["npc:arugal"] = {t="npc",n="Arugal",z="shadowfang",s="In Shadowfang Keep, Arugal commands the worgen he summoned against the Scourge. Madness and grief have made the former Dalaran wizard their self-proclaimed father, while his power threatens Silverpine Forest.",h="In Shadowfang Keep, Arugal commands the worgen he summoned against the Scourge.",sec={{t="A Desperate Summons",b="Before Lordaeron fell, Arugal belonged to the Kirin Tor. Some peers, including Dalar Dawnweaver, called him a charlatan who leaned on enchanted trinkets to make up for weak spellcraft. When the Scourge swept across the north during the Third War, Arugal searched for a weapon that could halt the undead. He used research by the late Dalaran mage Ur to pierce the veil between realms and summon the worgen. The ravenous beasts tore through the Scourge, but no one could contain their ferocity. Soon their hunger turned against innocent mortals.",sp=0},{t="Fall into Madness",b="The worgen slaughtered the Scourge, then turned on the wizards who summoned them. They besieged the ancestral seat of Baron Silverlaine, whose keep fell to their claws and fangs. Silverlaine and his retainers died in the massacre. Guilt shattered Arugal's mind, but he did not flee his creation. He adopted the beasts as his own offspring and renamed the fortress Shadowfang Keep. There he holds the ramparts, surrounded by ghostly victims and loyal hound-packs.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge of Silverpine",b="From Shadowfang Keep, Arugal's power reaches across the surrounding countryside. His dark sorcery blankets Pyrewood Village, where townsfolk live under a nocturnal curse, and fills the Deep Elem Mine with ravenous Moonrage beasts. The Forsaken see him as a threat they cannot tolerate. Sylvanas Windrunner's Deathstalkers and apothecaries plot the mad archmage's execution to secure the borders of their fledgling kingdom.",sp=1,bt={"q421.5"}}},faq={{q="Who is Arugal?",a="Arugal is a former human archmage of the Kirin Tor. During the Third War, he summoned the worgen to fight the Scourge. Overcome by what he had done, he withdrew to Shadowfang Keep and now leads packs of worgen as their self-proclaimed father.",al={"who is arugal","arugal backstory","shadowfang boss lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Arugal summon the worgen?",a="During the Third War, the Scourge threatened to overrun northern Lordaeron. Arugal sought a weapon to stop the undead and drew on the extraplanar research of the Dalaran mage Ur. He believed the savage beasts could destroy the Scourge, but lost control of them after summoning them.",al={"why worgen","why summon beasts","arugal worgen motive"},it="motive"},{q="Where does Arugal reside right now?",a="Arugal makes his lair at the pinnacle of Shadowfang Keep, an ancient fortress overlooking Pyrewood Village in southern Silverpine Forest. Fenrus, his monstrous wolf pet, guards him alongside loyal worgen and restless spirits.",al={"where is arugal","arugal location","find arugal"},it="place"},{q="What happened to Baron Silverlaine?",a="Baron Silverlaine was the noble lord who ruled the fortress and the village of Pyrewood. When Arugal's worgen besieged the castle, Silverlaine and his court were slaughtered. Their tortured ghosts haunt the keep's halls.",al={"baron silverlaine fate","who owned shadowfang","keep history"},it="history"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want Arugal dead?",a="Arugal's packs terrorize Silverpine Forest, attacking Forsaken scouts, ambushing patrols, and infecting servants of the Royal Apothecary Society. Sylvanas Windrunner sees the mad archmage as a direct threat to the security and expansion of the Undercity's borders.",al={"forsaken vs arugal","arugal must die quest","why kill arugal"},it="threat"},{q="What is the curse on Pyrewood Village?",a="Arugal's enchantments subjected Pyrewood Village's human inhabitants to the worgen curse. By daylight, the villagers appear human, but at nightfall they transform into vicious beasts bound to defend Arugal's territory.",al={"pyrewood curse","why are pyrewood villagers wolves","pyrewood arugal"}},{q="Whose side is Archmage Arugal on?",a="Arugal serves neither the Alliance nor the Horde. Once a member of Dalaran's Kirin Tor, he severed all former ties after falling into madness. Today he leads his own feral pack within Shadowfang Keep, considering the worgen his true children and violently rejecting both Kirin Tor envoys and the Forsaken.",al={"arugal faction","who does arugal serve","is arugal horde or alliance"},it="side",add="c709d248"},{q="What does Archmage Arugal want?",a="Consumed by guilt and madness after unleashing the worgen upon the world, Arugal now seeks to shelter, command, and expand his pack. He uses enchanted magic to bind the beasts to his will, spreading the worgen curse throughout Silverpine Forest to build his dark family and slaughter anyone who dares invade his domain.",al={"arugal goal","what is arugal trying to do","arugal motive"},it="wants",add="5a0ecd53"},{q="Why is Archmage Arugal in Shadowfang Keep?",a="After the summoned worgen broke past control, they assaulted the fortress belonging to Baron Silverlaine above Pyrewood Village. Driven mad by the catastrophe he orchestrated, Arugal adopted the ferocious beasts as his children, took over the ruined keep, and renamed it Shadowfang to rule his pack in secluded dominance.",al={"why is arugal here","why did arugal go to shadowfang","how did arugal get shadowfang keep"},it="why_here",add="127eccbf"},{q="Why is Archmage Arugal feared?",a="Arugal is infamous across Lordaeron for tapping into Ur's forbidden research to unleash the feral worgen upon the world. The curse he brought forth did not just slay the Scourge; it infected nearby lands, transformed peaceful villagers into bloodthirsty beasts, and turned an entire region into a nightmare under his erratic magical sway.",al={"why is arugal famous","arugal reputation","why is arugal dangerous"},it="fame",add="760497b6"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Arugal's worgen infest the road south of the Sepulcher, and Lady Sylvanas has ordered his execution to secure Silverpine Forest for the Forsaken.",["race:Undead"]="Arugal's beasts have killed several Deathstalkers and apothecaries. The Royal Apothecary Society needs his madness ended.",["class:Mage"]="Arugal shows the danger of reckless conjuration: Kirin Tor research became an uncontrollable nightmare."},kw={"arugal","kirin tor","pyrewood","shadowfang","silverlaine","silverpine","ur","worgen"},rel={"zone:shadowfang","zone:silverpine","topic:worgen","quest:1014","quest:99","subzone:pyrewood-village","npc:baron-silverlaine","npc:dalar-dawnweaver"},src={"Arugal"}}
E["npc:baron-silverlaine"] = {t="npc",n="Baron Silverlaine",z="shadowfang",s="Baron Silverlaine's spirit lingers in the Great Hall above Pyrewood Village. He once ruled Silverlaine Keep, until Archmage Arugal unleashed worgen upon the region and they slaughtered him.",h="Baron Silverlaine's spirit lingers in the Great Hall above Pyrewood Village.",sec={{t="The Fall of Silverlaine Keep",b="Baron Silverlaine ruled a noble estate in the southern hills of Silverpine. His fortress guarded the surrounding lands and kept them safe. That peace ended when Archmage Arugal summoned worgen to fight the rampaging Scourge and unleashed them upon the region. The feral beasts could not be controlled. They stormed the stronghold, overwhelmed its guards, and butchered the baron.",sp=0},{t="A Tormented Specter",b="Baron Silverlaine remains bound to the keep's ancient Great Hall. His restless ghost wanders among the wrecked dining tables where he once feasted. The cursed lord attacks intruders who enter his former home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Baron Silverlaine?",a="Baron Silverlaine ruled Silverlaine Keep, a fortress above Pyrewood Village. Worgen overran the fortress and killed him.",al={"baron silverlaine lore","who is silverlaine","who ruled shadowfang"},it="identity"},{q="Why is he haunting Shadowfang Keep?",a="Worgen unleashed by Archmage Arugal slaughtered Silverlaine in his own home. Cursed in death, his ghost remains bound to the dining hall of his keep and cannot move on.",al={"why is silverlaine a ghost","is silverlaine dead","silverlaine spirit"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Silverlaine attack trespassers?",a="Silverlaine's cursed spirit remains in his former home, where he attacks trespassers in the Great Hall.",al={"why does silverlaine attack","silverlaine ghost","silverlaine trespassers"}},{q="Where in the keep can he be found?",a="Baron Silverlaine haunts the Great Hall, once the keep's lavish dining room, which was wrecked when his estate fell.",al={"where is silverlaine","baron silverlaine location","silverlaine dining hall"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What was Shadowfang Keep called before the worgen attack?",a="Before the worgen attack, the fortress was called Silverlaine Keep, after the baron's noble family, who ruled it before Arugal took control.",al={"shadowfang original name","keep silverlaine lore","old name of shadowfang"},it="history"},{q="Did anyone in Silverlaine's family survive?",a="No account says whether anyone in Silverlaine's family survived. The accounts tell of the worgen assault and the baron's ghost, but say nothing about the rest of his household.",al={"silverlaine family","did silverlaines family live","silverlaine heirs"}},{q="Whose side is Baron Silverlaine on?",a="Baron Silverlaine fights for no one but himself and the tragic memories of his ruined estate. Though he was murdered when Archmage Arugal unleashed the feral worgen upon the castle, death has warped his spectral mind. Bound by a bitter curse, he strikes out indiscriminately at any living trespassers who enter his dining hall.",al={"baron silverlaine faction","who does silverlaine fight for","is baron silverlaine with arugal"},it="side",add="1b1b3783"},{q="What does Baron Silverlaine want?",a="Trapped as a vengeful phantom, Baron Silverlaine seeks only to drive away or slaughter anyone who dares invade his home. Tormented by his violent death, his spirit lashes out in relentless rage against those who disturb the ancient halls of his keep.",al={"what does silverlaine want","baron silverlaine goal","why does silverlaine attack"},it="wants",add="5d3ddd3d"},{q="Who is Baron Silverlaine tied to?",a="Baron Silverlaine's tragic fate is bound to Archmage Arugal. When Arugal summoned the extradimensional worgen to fight the Scourge, the beasts turned ravenous and besieged Silverlaine's keep. Arugal claimed the fortress as Shadowfang Keep, and the Baron's vengeful ghost haunts it still.",al={"silverlaine ties","who is silverlaine connected to","baron silverlaine and arugal"},it="ties",add="02c6a3ca"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For a human, Silverlaine's fate marks the fall of human noble authority on Gilneas's borders. His keep fell to the reckless magic of a Dalaran-trained wizard.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken crossing Silverpine, Silverlaine's specter is another remnant of the old aristocracy to clear before they can break Arugal's hold on the keep.",["class:Mage"]="For a mage, Silverlaine's fate warns of reckless magic. Archmage Arugal mishandled the summoner's art, destroying innocent lives and leaving lasting scars."},kw={"arugal","baron","ghost","great hall","keep","pyrewood","shadowfang","silverlaine","worgen"},rel={"zone:shadowfang","npc:arugal","topic:worgen","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Baron Silverlaine"}}
E["npc:commander-springvale"] = {t="npc",n="Commander Springvale",z="shadowfang",s="At Shadowfang Keep, Commander Springvale's spirit guards the halls where he fell. Once a devoted paladin and commander, he was slain with his men by Arugal's worgen and remains to haunt the castle.",h="At Shadowfang Keep, Commander Springvale's spirit guards the halls where he fell.",sec={{t="The Fallen Commander",b="Commander Springvale led the garrison at Shadowfang Keep in Silverpine Forest. Before the keep's ruin, he was an honorable paladin devoted to the Holy Light. After Lordaeron fell to the Scourge, he oversaw the fortress's security through those troubled days.",sp=0},{t="Arugal's Folly",b="Archmage Arugal summoned extraplanar worgen to strengthen Dalaran's failing ranks against the undead Scourge. The wild beasts soon escaped his control and descended on Shadowfang Keep. They slaughtered Baron Silverlaine and his entire guard. Springvale died in the halls he had sworn to protect, his service cut short.",sp=0},{t="An Endless Vigil",b="Death did not release Springvale. His ghost haunts the keep's council room with its spectral soldiers. He still wields paladin powers, including Holy Light and Hammer of Justice, against intruders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Commander Springvale in life?",a="Commander Springvale was a paladin devoted to the Holy Light and a commander at Shadowfang Keep. He died there when Arugal's worgen overran the fortress.",al={"springvale backstory","who is commander springvale","is springvale a paladin"},it="identity"},{q="How did Commander Springvale die?",a="Archmage Arugal summoned feral worgen to fight the Scourge, but the beasts turned on Shadowfang Keep's inhabitants. They killed Baron Silverlaine, Springvale, and the garrison.",al={"how did springvale die","who killed springvale","springvale death"},it="ruin"},{q="Why is Commander Springvale haunting Shadowfang Keep?",a="Springvale's spirit remains bound by his final oaths. His ghost wanders the halls to defend the ruins against all who enter.",al={"why is springvale a ghost","springvale motive","why does springvale fight"},it="why_here"},{q="What powers does Springvale use?",a="Springvale retains paladin abilities in undeath. He heals with Holy Light and stuns enemies with Hammer of Justice.",al={"why unholy magic","springvale unholy abilities","corrupted paladin"},it="power"},{q="Who was his master?",a="No record names the lord Springvale served. He is known as a commander who fell when Arugal's worgen overran Shadowfang Keep, the seat of Baron Silverlaine.",al={"springvale master","who did springvale serve","springvale and silverlaine"},it="ties"},{q="Where in the keep can he be found?",a="Commander Springvale's ghost haunts the fortified chambers deep within the keep, near the castle chapel and council rooms.",al={"springvale location","where is springvale","shadowfang springvale room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Commander Springvale on?",a="Commander Springvale serves no living master, nor is he allied with Archmage Arugal or the worgen that overrun the keep. In death his ghost haunts the council room of Shadowfang Keep with his spectral soldiers, striking down any living trespassers who enter the castle halls.",al={"springvale faction","who does springvale serve","springvale allegiance"},it="side",add="ccdbb916"},{q="What does Commander Springvale want?",a="Even in death, Commander Springvale remains bound to Shadowfang Keep, where he fell. Corrupted into undeath, he turns his wrath upon any intruders who dare set foot within its halls.",al={"springvale goal","what is springvale trying to do","springvale motive"},it="wants",add="5e96515a"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, Springvale shows how duty and sacred vows can become eternal torment when an honorable knight is bound to a corrupted grave.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can remember Springvale among the lost soldiers of Lordaeron and Gilneas. They fell to the reckless summonings meant to stop the Scourge, not to the Scourge itself.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde reclaiming Silverpine Forest, you can see laying Springvale's shade to rest as another step in purging the remnants of Arugal's tragic failure."},kw={"arugal","commander","ghost","paladin","shadowfang","silverlaine","silverpine","springvale","worgen"},rel={"zone:shadowfang","npc:baron-silverlaine","npc:arugal","topic:worgen","topic:light","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Commander Springvale (Classic)","Commander Springvale"}}
E["npc:deathstalker-vincent"] = {t="npc",n="Deathstalker Vincent",z="shadowfang",s="Inside Shadowfang Keep, Deathstalker Vincent lies slain by Arugal. The Forsaken scout entered the stronghold with Deathstalker Adamant to learn its defenses, but the mission ended before the Forsaken could attack.",h="Inside Shadowfang Keep, Deathstalker Vincent lies slain by Arugal.",sec={{t="A Scout's Fatal End",b="The Deathstalkers needed to learn Shadowfang Keep’s layout before the Forsaken could assault it. Vincent and Adamant slipped past the barricades into the fortress. Their mission failed: Adamant was captured and locked in a dungeon cell, while Vincent was brought before the keep’s master. Vincent refused to serve Arugal or yield to him. The mage executed him, leaving his body on the stone floor.",sp=0},{t="Arugal's Defiance",b="Arugal used Vincent’s death to defy the intruders in his keep. Facing the captive scout, the mad mage mocked the Forsaken and compared their intrusion with the failed efforts of his former Kirin Tor comrades. Arugal demanded Vincent’s blade and secrets for his own use. When Vincent refused, Arugal struck him down and declared that his remains would warn anyone who trespassed in his domain.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Deathstalker Vincent?",a="Vincent was a Forsaken scout in the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken’s intelligence arm. He and Deathstalker Adamant entered Shadowfang Keep to gather intelligence before the planned assault.",al={"who is vincent","vincent shadowfang keep","dead rogue shadowfang"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Vincent in Shadowfang Keep?",a="Vincent was captured during his reconnaissance and executed by Arugal after refusing to serve him or give up secrets. Arugal left his body where it fell.",al={"how did vincent die","why is vincent dead","who killed vincent"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is his partner, Deathstalker Adamant?",a="Deathstalker Adamant was captured alive and locked in a nearby dungeon cell, watched by a worgen guard.",al={"where is adamant","other deathstalker","adamant location"},it="ties"},{q="Why were the Deathstalkers sent to Shadowfang Keep?",a="Silverpine Forest is vital territory for Sylvanas and the Forsaken, while Arugal’s worgen hold Shadowfang Keep. Vincent and Adamant were sent to learn the fortress’s layout and defenses so the Forsaken could mount an effective attack.",al={"why are deathstalkers in shadowfang","forsaken mission shadowfang"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Deathstalker Vincent on?",a="Vincent is an operative of the Deathstalkers, the elite espionage and assassination order serving Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. He acts on behalf of the Undercity to scout enemy strongholds and eliminate threats to their fledgling kingdom.",al={"vincent faction","who does vincent serve","vincent allegiance"},it="side",add="ebb4e7c7"},{q="What does Deathstalker Vincent want?",a="Vincent sought to gather vital reconnaissance within Shadowfang Keep to enable an assault by the Forsaken. Defiant to the end, he refused Archmage Arugal's demand to turn traitor and pledge his blade to Arugal and his mysterious master.",al={"what was vincent trying to do","vincent goal","vincent objective"},it="wants",add="1f4e2f05"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, finding Vincent confirms the Forsaken commanders’ fears in Silverpine: the reconnaissance team failed, and the keep must be cleared by force.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, Vincent’s execution shows the danger faced by stealth operatives who infiltrate hostile strongholds alone."},kw={"arugal","deathstalker adamant","deathstalker vincent","shadowfang keep","silverpine forest","vincent","worgen"},rel={"quest:1098","zone:shadowfang","npc:arugal","topic:forsaken","topic:worgen","topic:horde"},src={"Deathstalker Vincent"}}
E["npc:fenrus-the-devourer"] = {t="npc",n="Fenrus the Devourer",z="shadowfang",s="In Shadowfang Keep, Fenrus the Devourer prowls the upper sanctum. Archmage Arugal keeps the enormous worg as a pet and guardian, its body swollen by unnatural magic. Intruders seeking the archmage's study must face the beast and its master.",h="In Shadowfang Keep, Fenrus the Devourer prowls the upper sanctum.",sec={{t="A Beast in the Master's Study",b="Fenrus the Devourer lurks outside Archmage Arugal's personal chambers deep within Shadowfang Keep. Unlike the worgen on the ramparts, Fenrus is a worg, swollen to enormous size. The beast prowls among the shelves, scrolls, and arcane apparatus in Arugal's private study. The archmage keeps Fenrus as both pet and guard against anyone who comes seeking his head.",sp=0},{t="Corrupted Might",b="Fenrus's unnatural bulk points to dark magic saturating the keep since Baron Silverlaine's downfall. Archmage Arugal or his unleashed worgen warped the creature through arcane or shadowy experiments, turning a native predator into a ravenous juggernaut. Fenrus is so feral and bound by magic that no hunter can charm or tame him.",sp=0},{t="Arugal's Watchful Eye",b="Disturbing Fenrus can mean death for the careless. When the worg spots an intruder, his ear-splitting howl rings through the fortress and draws Arugal's attention. The archmage projects his dark will into the chamber and summons voidwalkers to help Fenrus overwhelm and devour those who enter.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What kind of creature is Fenrus?",a="Fenrus is an exceptionally large worg, a wolf-like predator native to Lordaeron, rather than a bipedal worgen. His unnatural bulk and viciousness come from prolonged exposure to the dark magic practiced in Shadowfang Keep.",al={"is fenrus a worgen","fenrus creature type","fenrus wolf"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Fenrus be found?",a="Fenrus prowls the study chambers high inside Shadowfang Keep in Silverpine Forest. His lair lies directly along the approach to Archmage Arugal's inner redoubt.",al={"where is fenrus","fenrus location","fenrus room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can hunters tame Fenrus as a pet?",a="No. Though Fenrus is an ordinary beast by classification, hunters cannot tame him. His mind is broken and feral, bound to Archmage Arugal's dark will.",al={"can i tame fenrus","is fenrus tameable","taming fenrus"},gp=true},{q="Why does Arugal summon demons when Fenrus is attacked?",a="Arugal keeps Fenrus as a prized pet and the final guard before his sanctum. When Fenrus bellows as combat begins, Arugal intervenes and conjures voidwalkers into the chamber to overwhelm those threatening the beast.",al={"arugal voidwalkers","why does arugal help fenrus","fenrus voidwalker add"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Fenrus so much larger than normal worgs?",a="Fenrus's immense size is believed to come from Archmage Arugal's dark experiments, or from magical fallout from the worgen infestation overtaking the keep.",al={"why is fenrus huge","fenrus size lore","giant worg"},it="power"},{q="What happens across the dungeon when Fenrus is engaged?",a="When Fenrus enters combat, he unleashes a thunderous roar heard anywhere inside Shadowfang Keep. It alerts all to the battle outside Arugal's door.",al={"fenrus roar","fenrus howl across dungeon","loud roar sfk"},it="fame"},{q="Whose side is Fenrus on?",a="Fenrus is fiercely loyal to Archmage Arugal. As the sorcerer's personal beast and guardian, he serves whatever twisted will drives the master of Shadowfang Keep, attacking any intruder who trespasses into the upper sanctum without hesitation.",al={"fenrus faction","who does fenrus serve","fenrus loyalties"},it="side",add="b2b015f0"},{q="Why is Fenrus in Shadowfang Keep?",a="Fenrus prowls the main study directly adjoining Arugal's personal chambers. He acts as both a pet and a monstrous guard dog, placed there to tear apart anyone seeking to breach the inner sanctum of the archmage.",al={"why is fenrus here","fenrus location purpose","why does fenrus guard the study"},it="why_here",add="01e73d00"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Do not waste time trying to charm Fenrus. Shadowfang's dark arts have twisted his mind beyond repair, and the wild cannot bind him.",["class:Warlock"]="Archmage Arugal's voidwalkers show how deeply the former Dalaran mage has delved into forbidden shadow conjurations.",["class:Mage"]="Fenrus is a grim sign of Archmage Arugal's fall: he uses arcane arts to warp wild beasts into grotesque household guards."},kw={"arugal","fenrus","fenrus the devourer","shadowfang keep","silverpine","worg"},rel={"npc:arugal","zone:shadowfang","topic:worgen"},src={"Fenrus the Devourer"}}
E["npc:keeper-bel-dugur"] = {t="npc",n="Keeper Bel'dugur",z="shadowfang",s="In the Undercity, Keeper Bel'dugur commissions expeditions to recover dark tomes and magical artifacts for his people. The scholarly Forsaken works deep within the Apothecarium.",h="In the Undercity, Keeper Bel'dugur commissions expeditions to recover dark tomes and magical artifacts for...",sec={{t="A Collector of Dark Relics",b="Among the Apothecarium's vats and researchers, Keeper Bel'dugur sends adventurers to recover dangerous arcane and occult relics from across Azeroth. The Book of Ur, a legendary treatise on extra-dimensional beings, is locked away inside Shadowfang Keep and draws his keen interest. While many in the Undercity seek magical knowledge to cure or weaponize undeath, Bel'dugur's curated acquisitions seem chosen to uncover ancient, forbidden powers.",sp=0},{t="Hidden Loyalties",b="Keeper Bel'dugur's calm manner as an Undercity researcher conceals his loyalty to the apocalyptic Twilight's Hammer cult. The assignments he gives quietly advance the cult's esoteric aims, seeking foundational grimoires of summoning and void magic beneath the unsuspecting eyes of the Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Where can I find Keeper Bel'dugur?",a="Keeper Bel'dugur works in the Apothecarium, the alchemical district in the Undercity's southern lower ring.",al={"keeper bel'dugur location","where is beldugur","beldugur map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Bel'dugur want The Book of Ur?",a="The Book of Ur holds Dalaran mage Ur's foundational research on other dimensions and the feral worgen. Bel'dugur seeks its forbidden summoning principles for the dark schemes of his true masters.",al={"why book of ur","what does beldugur do with book of ur"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="Is Keeper Bel'dugur loyal to Lady Sylvanas?",a="Keeper Bel'dugur outwardly serves the Forsaken as an archivist and researcher, though hints in his investigations suggest his loyalties may lie elsewhere.",al={"is beldugur evil","beldugur faction","who does beldugur serve"},sp=2,it="side"},{q="What other tasks does he give adventurers?",a="Beyond the Book of Ur in Shadowfang Keep, Bel'dugur sends travelers after forgotten lore and forbidden tomes, including dark treatises tied to ancient rituals and forbidden knowledge.",al={"beldugur quests","keeper beldugur quests"},gp=true},{q="Who is Keeper Bel'dugur?",a="Keeper Bel'dugur is a Forsaken scholar stationed in the Apothecarium within the Undercity. While he presents himself as a quiet archivist collecting obscure tomes and forgotten lore for the Royal Apothecary Society, he pursues dangerous esoteric knowledge far beyond ordinary apothecary craft.",al={"who is bel'dugur","keeper beldugur lore","who is keeper beldugur"},it="identity",add="f8b2616f"},{q="What does Keeper Bel'dugur want?",a="Bel'dugur seeks forbidden arcane texts, occult secrets, and relics of dark power. He tasks adventurers with retrieving dangerous tomes such as The Book of Ur from Shadowfang Keep and other hidden digests to unlock perilous ancient magic.",al={"what does beldugur want","keeper beldugur motives","beldugur goal"},it="wants",add="3453eee6"},{q="Why is Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity?",a="Bel'dugur resides in the Apothecarium of the Undercity, an ideal sanctuary for those pursuing dark studies away from prying eyes. From the safety of the Forsaken capital, he directs wanderers to dangerous corners of the world to recover lost writings for his collection.",al={"why is bel'dugur in undercity","why is keeper beldugur here","beldugur location why"},it="why_here",add="43763d0f"},{q="Who is Keeper Bel'dugur tied to?",a="Beneath his role among the Forsaken in the Apothecarium, subtle clues and dialogue surrounding his forbidden research suggest ties to the secretive Twilight's Hammer cult, which covets world-shaking power and apocalyptic lore.",al={"keeper bel'dugur connections","who does beldugur work for","beldugur twilight's hammer"},sp=1,it="ties",add="5a26a87f"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you may see Bel'dugur as another scholarly Forsaken seeking forbidden knowledge to bolster your kingdom. His true ambitions serve a cause beyond the Banshee Queen's survivalist cause.",["class:Warlock"]="As a Warlock, you often cross paths with Bel'dugur's requests. His interests reach into dangerous grimoires, extraplanar summoning, and dark occultism."},kw={"apothecarium","bel'dugur","keeper beldugur","shadowfang","the book of ur","undercity"},rel={"subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","quest:1013","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:shadowfang","topic:forsaken"},src={"Keeper Bel'dugur"}}
E["quest:1013"] = {t="quest",n="The Book of Ur",z="shadowfang",s="Keeper Bel'dugur sends Horde champions into Shadowfang Keep for The Book of Ur. In the Undercity's Apothecarium, he seeks the treatise of Ur, a dead mage of Dalaran, for the Forsaken's use of its research into other planes.",h="Keeper Bel'dugur sends Horde champions into Shadowfang Keep for The Book of Ur.",sec={{t="A Relic of Extramundane Magic",b="Before the Third War destroyed Dalaran, the brilliant human wizard Ur devoted his scholarship to realms beyond Azeroth. The Kirin Tor strictly governed conjuration and contact with outer planes, but Ur studied beings from other dimensions, including the savage worgen. He hesitated to wield their alien powers, judging them dangerously uncontrollable. That restraint made his written legacy a coveted prize for those with fewer scruples.",sp=0},{t="The Fall into Dark Hands",b="Archmage Arugal took Ur's treatise and used its research before settling in Shadowfang Keep. Without Ur's reservations, Arugal summoned bloodthirsty worgen into Silverpine. Their curse consumed Pyrewood and the surrounding valleys. The volume now lies neglected in the keep's towers, watched by Arugal's feral pets.",sp=0},{t="The Forsaken's Ambition",b="Keeper Bel'dugur and the Royal Apothecary Society see Ur's fate as mortal frailty, not a warning against hubris. Bel'dugur believes conscience left Ur unable to act when danger came. The Forsaken seek the Book of Ur for the Undercity, intending to set aside its academic hesitation and harness its extradimensional lore. They mean to secure their survival and uphold Sylvanas Windrunner's rule across Lordaeron.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Ur?",a="Ur was a notable Dalaran mage who studied magic and other worlds before the Third War. He researched extradimensional creatures, including worgen, and died during the Scourge invasion of Dalaran.",al={"ur lore","who is ur","mage ur"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Book of Ur located?",a="The Book of Ur lies inside Shadowfang Keep, on a bookshelf in the chamber of Fenrus the Devourer, deep within the fortress.",al={"where is the book","book of ur location","shadowfang book location"},gp=true},{q="Who is Keeper Bel'dugur?",a="Keeper Bel'dugur is a Forsaken archivist and researcher in the Undercity's Apothecarium. He gathers dark, arcane, and extramundane lore to advance the power and survival of the Forsaken.",al={"beldugur","keeper bel dugur","quest giver"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why does the Forsaken want the book?",a="Bel'dugur and his cohort want Ur's research into extraplanar beings so the Forsaken can harness those powers. They believe Ur failed to survive the Scourge because conscience kept him from exploiting what he found, and the Undercity intends no such hesitation.",al={"why do forsaken want ur's book","undercity purpose book of ur"},it="motive"},{q="How did the book end up in Shadowfang Keep?",a="After Dalaran fell, Archmage Arugal acquired Ur's notes and used them to summon worgen into Lordaeron. He brought the research to Shadowfang Keep when he seized the fortress.",al={"how did arugal get the book","why is the book in sfk"},it="history"},{q="Is the Book of Ur related to the worgen curse?",a="Yes. Ur's research described the dimension where worgen originate. Arugal used the treatise to unleash the beasts upon Silverpine Forest, causing the infestation there.",al={"worgen origin book","book of ur worgen"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Book of Ur?",a="The Book of Ur is a prized arcane tome written by the late Dalaran mage Ur before the Scourge fell upon Lordaeron. Ur dedicated his studies to extradimensional realms and strange, otherworldly beasts—including the savage worgen. While Ur possessed immense magical knowledge, he ultimately refused to meddle too deeply with these lethal forces due to his moral conscience. To the Forsaken, who disdain such ethical hesitation, his research offers invaluable secrets into other worlds and dangerous planar entities.",al={"what is the book of ur","book of ur lore","contents of book of ur"},it="item",add="8665acc9"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Ur's Book is a grim part of Kirin Tor history. It shows how theoretical research into otherworldly beings could be twisted by unstable practitioners like Arugal into apocalyptic curses.",["class:Warlock"]="Ur's curiosity about what lies beyond mortal reality echoes a warlock's hunger for extraplanar knowledge. Bel'dugur says Ur failed because he lacked the nerve to wield what he discovered.",["race:Undead"]="Recovering the book serves Lady Sylvanas and the Royal Apothecary Society. It supports the Forsaken belief that survival means embracing forbidden lore without mortal squeamishness.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing Shadowfang Keep and securing Arugal's sources helps stabilize Silverpine Forest and curb the feral worgen menace near Horde-held lands."},kw={"apothecarium","arugal","bel'dugur","book of ur","dalaran","fenrus","kirin tor","shadowfang keep","worgen"},rel={"npc:keeper-bel-dugur","zone:shadowfang","subzone:apothecarium","zone:undercity","subzone:dalaran","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},m={start="Keeper Bel'dugur",level="26",faction="Horde",id=1013,ri={"The Book of Ur"}},src={"The Book of Ur (quest)"}}
E["quest:1014"] = {t="quest",n="Arugal Must Die",z="shadowfang",s="At the Sepulcher, Dalar Dawnweaver sends champions against Arugal. The rogue archmage holds Shadowfang Keep, and his worgen menace threatens the Forsaken’s hold on Silverpine Forest.",h="At the Sepulcher, Dalar Dawnweaver sends champions against Arugal.",sec={{t="A Thorn in the Dark Lady's Side",b="Shadowfang Keep rises above the woods, where Archmage Arugal commands the worgen. The Forsaken have made the Sepulcher their base, but Silverpine Forest remains dangerous and fiercely contested. Driven mad by guilt and dark sorcery, Arugal unleashed the feral worgen upon Lordaeron. His ravenous beasts roam the forest paths and hinder Lady Sylvanas Windrunner’s efforts to secure the region.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Beast at the Neck",b="Dalar Dawnweaver knows that hunting worgen across the forest will not end the danger. Their source lies inside Shadowfang Keep. You must breach the old stronghold, fight through Arugal’s worgen brood, and confront the mad wizard in his aerie. His severed head is proof of his death, and his defeat can break his hold over the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want Arugal dead?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver wants Arugal dead because his worgen overrun Silverpine Forest. Until the mage is slain, the Forsaken cannot make the region a secure stronghold.",al={"why kill arugal","dalar dawnweaver goal","arugal target"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Arugal be found?",a="Archmage Arugal can be found in Shadowfang Keep, high above southern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is arugal","arugal location","find arugal"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What proof is required to complete the mission?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver requires the severed Head of Arugal as proof of the wizard’s death.",al={"what does dalar need","arugal head quest","proof of death"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What threat does Arugal pose to the Horde?",a="Arugal commands legions of cursed worgen that harass Horde forces and threaten Forsaken control throughout Silverpine Forest. He also wields potent offensive magic.",al={"why is arugal dangerous","worgen threat silverpine","is arugal a threat"},it="threat"},{q="Who does Dalar Dawnweaver serve?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver serves Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. He works from the Sepulcher to strengthen Forsaken control across Lordaeron.",al={"who does dawnweaver work for","sepulcher leadership"},it="side"},{q="What happens after Arugal is defeated?",a="Arugal’s death breaks his magical grip over Silverpine, letting the Forsaken extend their hold across western Lordaeron without fear of his coordinated worgen packs.",al={"after arugal dies","result of arugal death"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the Head of Arugal for?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver demands the severed head of Archmage Arugal as undeniable proof that the mad wizard's reign over Shadowfang Keep has ended. Beyond simple confirmation of the kill, Dalar intends to personally examine the remains to unravel and eradicate the foul, lingering magic Arugal cast over Silverpine Forest, ensuring his curse can no longer threaten the Forsaken.",al={"head of arugal purpose","why take arugals head","what does dalar do with arugal head"},it="item",add="375fc177"},{q="Who is Archmage Arugal?",a="Archmage Arugal was once a wizard of the Kirin Tor in Dalaran. Driven to madness, he unleashed the ferocious worgen upon Lordaeron to combat the Scourge, only to lose control of the beasts. Retreating to Shadowfang Keep, he slaughtered Baron Silverlaine and claimed the fortress as his own, adopting the feral monsters as his cursed 'children' and terrorizing Silverpine Forest ever since.",al={"who is arugal","shadowfang keep boss arugal","why is arugal in shadowfang"},it="target",add="62d569dd"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you help secure your southwestern border and protect the routes between the Sepulcher and the Undercity.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help break an entrenched wizard and open vital roads, showing the Horde’s growing reach in the Eastern Kingdoms.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you face a Kirin Tor mage warped by otherworldly summons, a warning of arcane hubris."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","head of arugal","sepulcher","shadowfang keep","silverpine","sylvanas","worgen"},rel={"npc:arugal","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","zone:shadowfang","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="27",faction="Horde",id=1014,ri={"Head of Arugal"}},src={"Arugal Must Die"}}
E["quest:1098"] = {t="quest",n="Deathstalkers in Shadowfang",z="shadowfang",s="In Shadowfang Keep, Deathstalkers Adamant and Vincent have gone missing. High Executor Hadrec sends Horde adventurers inside to find the reconnaissance agents. Their intelligence is needed to prepare a Forsaken assault against Archmage Arugal and his worgen packs.",h="In Shadowfang Keep, Deathstalkers Adamant and Vincent have gone missing.",sec={{t="Into the Worgen Den",b="Silverpine Forest remains contested, and Archmage Arugal's worgen hold Shadowfang Keep. The Forsaken at the Sepulcher seek to break his siege on their southern borders. High Executor Hadrec sent Deathstalkers Adamant and Vincent into the fortress to chart its defenses. Days pass without word, and Hadrec grows desperate for their reports. He sends Horde champions into the stronghold to recover the agents and salvage the operation.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Discovery",b="The lower ramparts reveal the cost of the infiltration. Deathstalker Adamant survives in captivity and helps unbar the courtyard gates. Vincent met a brutal end; his broken corpse lies motionless within the keep, and his intelligence is lost in its dark halls. A small trinket remains clenched in his fingers, a last sign of a spy who gave his life for the Dark Lady's conquest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why were Deathstalkers sent to Shadowfang Keep?",a="High Executor Hadrec ordered the infiltration to gather tactical intelligence on Archmage Arugal's forces and fortifications before the Forsaken commit troops to an assault on Shadowfang Keep.",al={"why send spies to shadowfang","hadrec mission purpose","deathstalker goal shadowfang"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are Deathstalkers Adamant and Vincent?",a="Adamant and Vincent are elite Forsaken operatives and advance scouts. They belong to the Deathstalkers, the Undercity's espionage and assassination branch, and were sent to map Shadowfang Keep and observe its worgen defenses.",al={"who are adamant and vincent","adamant and vincent lore"},it="people"},{q="What happened to Deathstalker Vincent?",a="Vincent has not reported back from Shadowfang Keep. Hadrec needs someone to enter the fortress and discover what happened to him.",al={"did vincent die","where is vincent","vincent fate"},sp=1},{q="What role does Deathstalker Adamant play inside the keep?",a="Adamant is one of the missing Deathstalkers sent to gather intelligence inside Shadowfang Keep. His situation is learned during the search.",al={"what does adamant do","deathstalker adamant role"},sp=1},{q="Where does this mission begin?",a="High Executor Hadrec gives the assignment at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, where he is stationed as the Forsaken military commander.",al={"where to get deathstalkers in shadowfang","quest giver deathstalkers in shadowfang"},it="arrival"},{q="Why does the Forsaken leadership want Shadowfang Keep cleared?",a="Archmage Arugal unleashes violent worgen packs across Silverpine Forest from Shadowfang Keep. They constantly threaten Forsaken holdings, supply lines, and the security of Lordaeron.",al={"why attack shadowfang","forsaken beef with arugal"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec need you to find the Deathstalkers?",a="High Executor Hadrec is preparing a major Forsaken assault against Shadowfang Keep, but his entire strategy hinges on vital intelligence. He sent Deathstalkers Adamant and Vincent ahead to scout the fortress, but days have passed without word. Without their reconnaissance on the enemy's strength and defenses, any direct offensive would be marching blindly into slaughter.",al={"why does hadrec want this done","hadrec motive shadowfang","why search for the deathstalkers"},it="motive",add="7d643f75"},{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec send you instead of his own troops?",a="The Sepulcher's standing forces are stretched thin holding the line across Silverpine, and committing an army to infiltrate Shadowfang without intelligence would invite disaster. Hadrec needs a resourceful, capable adventurer who can slip past the keep's outer perimeter, track down his missing elite scouts, and provide whatever aid they require to salvage the mission.",al={"why send me shadowfang","why not use deathstalkers or guards","why me hadrec"},it="why_me",add="cc510862"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming Silverpine from Arugal's beasts is essential to securing Lordaeron. The missing scouts show the danger of that struggle.",["class:Rogue"]="The Deathstalkers' disappearance shows the risks of reconnaissance behind fortified enemy lines.",["faction:Horde"]="High Executor Hadrec relies on Horde champions to support Forsaken operations when conventional troops cannot breach Arugal's cursed fortress."},kw={"adamant","arugal","deathstalkers in shadowfang","hadrec","sepulcher","shadowfang keep","silverpine","vincent"},rel={"npc:high-executor-hadrec","npc:deathstalker-vincent","zone:shadowfang","quest:1886","quest:448"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",["end"]="Deathstalker Vincent",level="25",faction="Horde",id=1098},src={"Deathstalkers in Shadowfang"}}
E["zone:shadowfang"] = {t="dungeon",n="Shadowfang Keep",z="shadowfang",s="In southern Silverpine, Shadowfang Keep shelters the rogue Kirin Tor wizard Archmage Arugal and the worgen he summoned. The old Silverlaine estate now holds feral beasts and the phantoms of its slaughtered defenders, while nearby Pyrewood Village remains bound to a horrifying curse.",h="In southern Silverpine, Shadowfang Keep shelters the rogue Kirin Tor wizard Archmage Arugal and the worgen he...",sec={{t="Fall of the Silverlaine Dynasty",b="Shadowfang Keep was once Silverlaine Keep, a noble seat defended by the pious Commander Springvale. During the Third War, the Scourge swept through Lordaeron and Dalaran's wizards fell in droves. Desperate to stem the rising dead, Archmage Arugal defied the Kirin Tor leadership and turned to the research of the wizard Ur. He summoned extra-dimensional worgen to turn the tide. The beasts savaged the undead, then slipped beyond mortal control and stormed southern Silverpine. Baron Silverlaine and his entire court were massacred, doomed to haunt the stone halls beside the feral monsters that overran their home.",sp=0},{t="Arugal's Children",b="Broken by guilt and madness, Arugal withdrew behind the blood-stained battlements. He called the ravenous wolf-men his beloved children and named the castle Shadowfang Keep. In its stone roosts, lupine packs and shadowy hounds thrive under trainers such as Wolf Master Nandos, watched by Arugal's massive lupine beast, Fenrus the Devourer. The curse did not halt at the walls. Nearby Pyrewood Village remains trapped in a horrifying nocturnal cycle: its people walk as men by day and hunt as ravenous worgen beneath the moon, bound to the mad archmage on the heights above.",sp=0},{t="The Forsaken Strike",b="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner saw Arugal as a dire threat to her dominion in Silverpine Forest and sent the Royal Apothecary Society and elite Deathstalkers to find the source of the worgen curse. Infiltration teams suffered brutal losses in the dungeons, but Horde heroes answering the call from the Sepulcher eventually break into the highest tower. When they strike down Arugal, the pack loses its master. The mind directing the beasts' spread through the wilderness is severed, and his head becomes proof of Lordaeron's vengeance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happens when Archmage Arugal is defeated?",a="Slaying Arugal removes the central force controlling the worgen packs in southern Silverpine. On Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's orders, Horde adventurers take his severed head to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher. The feral beasts and ghostly remnants in the keep and surrounding woods remain a danger to travelers.",al={"kill arugal outcome","arugal dead lore","what happens after arugal dies"},sp=1,it="next_step",nx={42,43}},{q="Why did Arugal summon the worgen?",a="During the Third War, Dalaran's armies suffered disastrous defeats against the Scourge, and fallen wizards kept rising as undead soldiers for the Lich King. Seeking a weapon to turn the tide, Arugal used the research of the wizard Ur to summon extra-dimensional worgen, believing their savagery could halt the Scourge.",al={"why worgen summoned","arugal motive","dalaran worgen summon"},it="motive"},{q="Who was Baron Silverlaine?",a="Baron Silverlaine was the human nobleman who ruled the keep and oversaw nearby Pyrewood before the Third War. When Arugal's summoned beasts escaped control, they stormed the stronghold and killed the baron, his household, and his guards. Silverlaine's vengeful ghost still haunts the great dining halls, cursed to walk beside the monsters that slew him.",al={"baron silverlaine lore","original lord of shadowfang"},it="identity"},{q="Why are Pyrewood Village villagers friendly during the day?",a="Arugal's dark magic left the people of nearby Pyrewood Village human, clear-minded, and peaceful toward Alliance travelers by day. At sundown, the curse takes hold and transforms the entire population into savage worgen loyal to the mad archmage in the keep.",al={"pyrewood humans","pyrewood curse","why pyrewood turns worgen"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Commander Springvale?",a="Commander Springvale was a paladin and the military officer responsible for defending Silverlaine Keep. When the worgen overran the stronghold, he fought to the death. His restless spirit still patrols the upper hallways, clinging to martial duty even in undeath.",al={"springvale lore","ghostly paladin boss"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Book of Ur?",a="The Book of Ur holds the research of Ur, an archmage of Dalaran who studied extra-dimensional entities, including the worgen. Arugal used the writings to make his disastrous summons. The Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity seeks the book to understand the wolf-creatures and their strange magic.",al={"book of ur quest","ur lore"},it="item"},{q="What is Shadowfang Keep?",a="Shadowfang Keep is a haunted castle perched on the high bluffs of southern Silverpine Forest, overlooking Pyrewood Village. Originally known as Silverlaine Keep, it once served as an Alliance stronghold guarding the borders near Gilneas. Today, it stands corrupted and shrouded in dark mists, serving as the stronghold for Archmage Arugal and his feral worgen progeny.",al={"what is shadowfang keep","tell me about shadowfang","shadowfang keep lore"},it="place",add="4bfedcc6",nx={8,9}},{q="Who built Shadowfang Keep?",a="The fortress was the seat of Baron Silverlaine, a noble whose family long held lordship over the surrounding lands and Pyrewood Village before the Third War. Under his rule, it stood as a proud human bastion, guarded by Commander Springvale and sworn soldiers of the realm.",al={"who built shadowfang keep","origin of shadowfang","who made shadowfang"},it="origin",add="1d3b32c5"},{q="Why is Shadowfang Keep full of worgen?",a="When the summoned worgen broke free from Kirin Tor control, they rampaged through the forest and laid siege to the castle. They butchered Baron Silverlaine and his household. Driven mad by guilt over what he had unleashed, Archmage Arugal adopted the beasts as his own 'children,' claimed the ruin for himself, and renamed it Shadowfang Keep.",al={"why are there worgen here","shadowfang keep worgen why","why worgen inside"},it="threat",add="efb02893"},{q="Why is the Horde interested in this castle?",a="The worgen roaming out of the keep are an unchecked plague threatening the Forsaken's hold over Silverpine Forest. From their base at the Sepulcher, Forsaken leaders realized that as long as Arugal commands his lupine horrors from the castle heights, the surrounding lands will never be secure.",al={"why does the horde care about shadowfang","horde interest shadowfang","why come to shadowfang keep"},it="arrival",add="7d419eb0",nx={11,12}},{q="Who sent me here?",a="Forsaken commanders at the Sepulcher ordered the assault to eliminate Arugal and discover the fate of their missing scouts. Meanwhile, the Royal Apothecary Society in the Undercity dispatched agents to retrieve Ur's magical research from the archmage's library.",al={"who sent me to shadowfang","shadowfang keep quest giver","who wants arugal dead"},it="motive",add="d6cbfc07"},{q="Is this Forsaken land now?",a="The Forsaken claim northern Silverpine, but their hold on the south is hotly contested. Shadowfang Keep remains firmly under Arugal's dominion, while lingering Scourge, feral beasts, and surviving human settlements dispute the Dark Lady's rule across the region.",al={"is silverpine forsaken land","does sylvanas own this","forsaken territory shadowfang"},it="conflict",add="a794fece"},{q="Who is in charge in Shadowfang Keep?",a="The castle answers entirely to Archmage Arugal. Driven mad by the Third War, he rules the upper towers flanked by his monstrous worgen and massive pet worg, Fenrus, commanding the keep through dark sorcery.",al={"who rules shadowfang keep","who is in charge inside","shadowfang master"},it="in_charge",add="b918d1de",nx={14,15}},{q="Is Arugal the boss of the keep?",a="Yes. Arugal is the master of Shadowfang Keep. He orchestrates the worgen infestation across Silverpine and sits at the pinnacle of the keep's tower as its ultimate authority.",al={"is arugal the boss","final boss shadowfang","arugal master"},it="leader",add="ecad974c"},{q="Was anyone in charge before him?",a="Baron Silverlaine ruled the keep when it was an Alliance redoubt. He and his family governed the castle until Arugal's worgen breached the walls and slaughtered everyone inside during the Third War.",al={"who ruled before arugal","previous master of shadowfang","past lord of the keep"},it="history",add="3b086809"},{q="Where do the worgen come from?",a="They are ravenous extra-dimensional beings torn from another plane. Desperate to stop the Scourge during the Third War, Arugal turned to the forbidden research of the Dalaran mage Ur and summoned these otherworldly beasts into Azeroth.",al={"where did worgen come from","origin of the worgen","worgen source"},it="threat",add="7f02160f",nx={17,18}},{q="Did Arugal summon the worgen alone?",a="Arugal performed the summoning against the explicit advice of his peers in Dalaran's Kirin Tor. Relying heavily on the writings in the Book of Ur, he forced the entities across planar boundaries.",al={"did arugal act alone","who helped summon worgen","arugal summoning"},it="history",add="4fa8e666"},{q="Can the worgen be controlled?",a="Barely, and only through dark magic. Though summoned to serve as allies against the undead, they turned immediately on their summoners. Arugal manages to direct some of them only because his broken mind treats them as family, using enchantments to enforce fragile obedience.",al={"can worgen be controlled","controlling the worgen","are worgen tame"},it="danger",add="a6a018be"},{q="What happened to the Deathstalkers Adamant and Vincent?",a="Deathstalkers Adamant and Vincent slipped into Shadowfang Keep on orders from the Sepulcher to scout Arugal's strength. They were captured by the keep's defenders; Vincent was imprisoned and executed in the courtyard, while Adamant lies trapped within the dungeons waiting for rescue.",al={"adamant and vincent","what happened to the deathstalkers","forsaken scouts shadowfang"},sp=1,it="purpose",add="24ed31c3",nx={20,21}},{q="Why were the Deathstalkers sent into Shadowfang Keep?",a="Forsaken command needed precise intelligence on the beastly infestation threatening their southern front. Adamant and Vincent were tasked with infiltrating the keep, determining Arugal's true numbers, and paving the way for a decisive strike.",al={"why send deathstalkers","scouting shadowfang","deathstalker mission"},it="motive",add="cc7bdeae"},{q="Are the Deathstalkers still alive?",a="Vincent is dead, slain after his capture. Adamant, however, remains imprisoned deep within the keep's lower holding cells, alive enough to assist any Horde adventurers who break through to him.",al={"are vincent and adamant alive","did deathstalkers survive","deathstalker fate"},sp=1,it="threat",add="4cfa60a4"},{q="What are Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the elite covert assassins and rogues of the Forsaken. Specializing in stealth, espionage, and sudden death, they operate as the silent daggers of the Undercity across Lordaeron's frontiers.",al={"what is a deathstalker","who are deathstalkers","forsaken deathstalkers"},it="other",add="c6ee2849",nx={23,24}},{q="Who do the Deathstalkers answer to?",a="They answer through a strict chain of command governed by Forsaken officers and commanders stationed across the territories, ultimately serving the will of the Undercity's ruling council.",al={"deathstalker leadership","who commands deathstalkers","who leads deathstalkers"},it="leader",add="40c5e48b"},{q="Do the Deathstalkers work for Sylvanas directly?",a="Yes. Every Deathstalker is sworn to the Banshee Queen, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. They form her personal intelligence network, rooting out threats to her free-willed undead throughout Lordaeron.",al={"do deathstalkers serve sylvanas","sylvanas deathstalkers","deathstalkers banshee queen"},it="ties",add="63a10ab0"},{q="Why is everyone sending me into Shadowfang Keep?",a="Because the Forsaken's initial reconnaissance completely collapsed with the capture of their elite Deathstalkers. Arugal's lair is too treacherous for standard infantry, requiring proven adventurers who can cut through both beasts and vengeful spirits.",al={"why send me to shadowfang","why am i doing this","why hero shadowfang"},it="why_me",add="f68cd02f",nx={26,27}},{q="Am I the only one left to do it?",a="Forsaken resources in Silverpine are stretched razor-thin battling Rot Hide gnolls, Scourge holdouts, and Dalaran patrols. With their own advance scouts compromised, you and your allies are the only force capable of breaching the keep.",al={"am i the only one","no one else to clear shadowfang","only choice"},it="purpose",add="ebbfbfb0"},{q="Did others try to breach the keep before me?",a="Yes. Beyond the failed Deathstalker scouts, Kirin Tor investigators such as Sorcerer Ashcrombe entered the keep to evaluate Arugal, only to end up captured or trapped within its cursed halls.",al={"did others try shadowfang","previous attempts shadowfang","who tried before"},it="history",add="0f7e4add"},{q="What happened to Silverpine Forest?",a="Silverpine was once a verdant realm of towering silver-barked pines guarded by the Alliance. When the Scourge swept Lordaeron during the Third War, the plague withered the woods, crops were burned, and its people were massacred or driven behind the Greymane Wall.",al={"silverpine history","what happened to silverpine","why is silverpine like this"},it="history",add="13386e7c",nx={29,30}},{q="Was Silverpine Lordaeron land?",a="Yes. Silverpine formed the rugged western edge of the Kingdom of Lordaeron, bordering Gilneas to the south. Its estates and settlements were bound to the Alliance before the plague shattered the kingdom.",al={"was this lordaeron","silverpine lordaeron history","did lordaeron own silverpine"},it="place",add="7c8f83a0"},{q="Why is Silverpine Forest so empty now?",a="Between the Scourge invasion, Gilneas closing its great wall, and Arugal's rampaging worgen curse, the living population was slaughtered, cursed, or fled abroad. The few who remain cling desperately to contested hamlets like Pyrewood.",al={"why is silverpine empty","deserted silverpine","silverpine ruins why"},it="ruin",add="91da6ffd"},{q="Why did Arugal bring worgen to Silverpine in the first place?",a="When the undead Scourge marched south, Dalaran's wizards were dying in droves, only to rise again in the Lich King's service. Arugal believed extra-dimensional summoned allies could overwhelm the undead where conventional mortal armies had failed.",al={"why bring worgen to silverpine","reason arugal summoned worgen","why summon worgen here"},it="history",add="2ee73ad9",nx={32,33}},{q="Who was Arugal trying to stop?",a="He summoned them specifically to annihilate the undead armies of the Scourge, which were swelling by slaughtering and raising every soldier and wizard that fell in battle.",al={"who was arugal fighting","arugal enemy","who did arugal summon worgen against"},it="threat",add="671a79f5"},{q="Did Arugal's plan work against the Scourge?",a="Tactically, yes—the worgen effortlessly tore the undead apart. But strategically, it was a catastrophe. The feral wolf-men could not be controlled, turned upon human soldiers and wizards alike, and spread a deadly curse across the region.",al={"did worgen beat the scourge","did the summoning work","worgen success vs scourge"},it="conflict",add="eeb57b84"},{q="Are the worgen in the keep the same ones that overran Pyrewood?",a="Yes. Arugal's packs, including the Shadowfang and Moonrage packs, share the same cursed origin. The beasts stalking the castle halls are Arugal's personal brood, closely tied to the curse afflicting the villagers below.",al={"are shadowfang worgen from pyrewood","pyrewood worgen shadowfang","same worgen pack"},it="threat",add="2bfe7e75",nx={35,36}},{q="What happened to the Pyrewood villagers?",a="The villagers survived the Third War only to be ensnared by Arugal's dark magic. Though they appear as normal humans during daylight, sunset transforms them into savage, bloodthirsty worgen loyal to the mad archmage.",al={"what happened to pyrewood people","fate of pyrewood","pyrewood townsfolk"},it="people",add="b78b86f3"},{q="Are the Pyrewood villagers cursed too?",a="Yes. They are victims of the lycanthropic worgen curse. By day, they retain their minds and trade peacefully with Alliance wanderers; by night, the curse strips their humanity away, turning them into ravenous beasts.",al={"is pyrewood cursed","pyrewood curse","are villagers infected"},it="danger",add="39fbc1b5"},{q="Who are the ghosts inside Shadowfang?",a="They are the restless spirits of Baron Silverlaine, Commander Springvale, and the castle's former household. Slain in the surprise worgen onslaught, their souls remain bound to the ruined stones by torment and grief.",al={"ghosts in shadowfang","who are the spirits in sfk","specters shadowfang"},it="threat",add="d6e89a88",nx={38,39}},{q="Are the ghosts the old servants of the keep?",a="Yes. From ghostly cooks and shadowy attendants to former guardsmen, the spectral defenders wandering the halls are the slaughtered retainers who once attended Baron Silverlaine in life.",al={"are ghosts former servants","castle servants ghosts","silverlaine servants"},it="residents",add="0a399272"},{q="Why can't the ghosts rest?",a="The sheer horror of their slaughter, combined with the heavy shadow magic saturating the keep, prevents their release. In their perpetual anguish, they lash out with unholy hatred at any living trespasser who disturbs their graves.",al={"why are ghosts restless","why do spirits haunt shadowfang","unrest ghosts shadowfang"},it="threat",add="3f532512"},{q="Is Arugal working for the Scourge?",a="No. Arugal despises the Scourge; he summoned the worgen precisely to destroy them. Though he has gone mad, his loyalty belongs to his 'children' rather than the Lich King.",al={"is arugal scourge","arugal working for scourge","does arugal serve the scourge"},it="other",add="59c03d52",nx={41}},{q="Does the Lich King control Arugal?",a="No. Arugal's madness is entirely self-inflicted, born of guilt and planar magic rather than the telepathic grip of the Frozen Throne. He operates independently as master of his own dark domain.",al={"does lich king control arugal","lich king arugal","arugal mind control"},it="in_charge",add="99eb22e3"},{q="Does the curse end after Arugal is dead?",a="No. Slaying Arugal decapitates the leadership of Shadowfang Keep, but the worgen curse has already infected the blood of mortals across the forest. The affliction persists long after the archmage falls.",al={"does the worgen curse end","will worgen curse vanish","is pyrewood cured"},sp=1,it="threat",add="501c4a9b"},{q="Will the Forsaken take Shadowfang Keep?",a="For now, the Forsaken are content with eliminating the threat to their southern border and recovering the Book of Ur. The ruin remains a grim, haunted shell overlooking the woods rather than a garrisoned outpost.",al={"will forsaken take shadowfang","do forsaken capture shadowfang","who controls sfk after"},it="next_step",add="6cb01af1"},{q="How did I end up in Shadowfang Keep?",a="You followed the trail of terror through Silverpine Forest to the bluffs overlooking Pyrewood Village. If you serve the Horde, you were likely directed south from the Sepulcher or Undercity to investigate the worgen menace choking the region. If you fight for the Alliance, rumors of the cursed woods, lost holy relics, or the fallen Kirin Tor brought you deep into hostile Forsaken territory. Climbing the winding crags beyond Pyrewood's gates, you pushed past ravenous wolf-beasts and battered through the keep's ancient gateway to enter the lair of the mad archmage.",al={"how did i get here","how do i reach shadowfang keep","how did i find this place"},it="arrival",add="3f22b397"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Shadowfang Keep?",a="Your ultimate goal is to fight through the haunted halls and strike down Archmage Arugal, ending his twisted reign over Silverpine. Along the way, you must cut down the worgen stalking the courtyards and put down the restless spirits of Baron Silverlaine and his slain household. If acting on behalf of the Forsaken, you are tasked with recovering the Book of Ur and discovering the fate of missing Deathstalkers sent inside. Alliance champions, paladins, and warlocks seek lost artifacts of power, holy armaments, and retribution against the dark magic poisoning the land.",al={"what am i doing here","why am i here","what is my goal in shadowfang keep"},it="purpose",add="31a8c552"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Forsaken see Arugal's encroaching packs as an immediate danger to their fledgling territory in Silverpine. Deathstalker operatives and the Royal Apothecary Society make the keep a priority target.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, Shadowfang's tragedy warns what can happen when a Kirin Tor wizard meddles with extra-dimensional summoning beyond mortal control.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may be drawn to the keep's dark energies, voidwalkers, and fell sorceries, and to the search for ancient relics such as the Orb of Soran'ruk.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you may see Commander Springvale's restless spirit as a sorrowful reminder of fallen paladin defenders whose sacred oaths were warped by death."},kw={"arugal","fenrus","pyrewood","sfk","shadowfang","silverlaine","silverpine","springvale","worgen"},rel={"npc:arugal","npc:baron-silverlaine","npc:commander-springvale","quest:1014","quest:1013","subzone:pyrewood-village","zone:silverpine","topic:worgen"},m={levels="22-30"},src={"Shadowfang Keep (Classic)","Shadowfang Keep"}}
